<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)ai.reyes.thetin</string>
    </array>
    <key>com.apple.developer.devicecheck.appattest-environment</key>
    <string>development</string>
    <key>com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers</key>
    <array>
        <string>iCloud.ai.reyes.thetin</string>
    </array>
    <!--
      MULTI-DEVICE SYNC IS NOT LIVE YET. To turn it on, add <string>CloudKit</string> to the array
      below (the container iCloud.ai.reyes.thetin already exists for CloudDocuments; CloudKit
      enables the database side of the SAME container — no new container is needed) and define
      TIN_CLOUDKIT in project.yml so SyncService.makeEngine() returns a real engine:

        <key>com.apple.developer.icloud-services</key>
        <array>
            <string>CloudDocuments</string>
            <string>CloudKit</string>
        </array>

      Left off on purpose. Applying it requires the CloudKit capability on App ID ai.reyes.thetin
      in the developer portal, which has NOT been done — an applied entitlement without the portal
      capability fails to sign. Inert, SyncService reports `unavailable`, which is the same code
      path as signed-out, and the app behaves exactly as it does today.

      The full five-step order — and why doing it out of order fails SILENTLY for every TestFlight
      tester — is in CLAUDE.md, "Rolling out iCloud sync". Read it before flipping this.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.developer.icloud-services</key>
    <array>
        <string>CloudDocuments</string>
    </array>
    <key>com.apple.developer.ubiquity-container-identifiers</key>
    <array>
        <string>iCloud.ai.reyes.thetin</string>
    </array>
    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>group.ai.reyes.thetin</string>
    </array>
    <key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
    <array>
        <string>applinks:thetinapp.com</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
